<title>NEW ZEALAND: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT LIST (961210)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 10 Dec 96 - Nationalist New Zealand First Party leader    *</p>
<p> *		 Winston Peters said he would join a coalition *</p>
<p> *		 with the conservative National Party, ending  *</p>
<p> *		 two months of uncertainty since October's     *</p>
<p> *		 general election. Peters will be deputy prime *</p>
<p> *		 minister. The deal gives National Party leader*</p>
<p> *		 Jim Bolger a new three-year term as prime     *</p>
<p> *		 minister.						 *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>				  - - - - - -</p>
<p>Governor-General (Sworn in 21 Mar 1996)...Michael HARDIE BOYS</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING NATIONAL PARTY GOVERNMENT</p>
<p>(Formed 1 Nov 1990, reshuffled Feb 29, 1996)</p>
<p> Prime Minister.....................................Jim BOLGER</p>
<p>(also Minister in charge of the New Zealand</p>
<p>Security Intelligence Service)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister............................Don MCKINNON</p>
<p>(also Minister for Foreign Affairs &amp; Trade,</p>
<p>Pacific Island Affairs)</p>
<p>				- - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>Agriculture, Deputy Minister of Finance,</p>
<p>    Responsible for Contact Energy..............Lockwood SMITH</p>
<p>Attorney General, State Services,</p>
<p>Serious Fraud Office, Audit Department,</p>
<p>    Defence, Corrections, War Pensions...............Paul EAST</p>
<p> Conservation......................................Simon UPTON</p>
<p>Crown Health Enterprises, Associate Minister</p>
<p>    of Education................................. Bill ENGLISH</p>
<p> Education, Employment............................Wyatt CREECH</p>
<p>Environment, Research, Science and Technology,</p>
<p>    Crown Research Institutes, Radio NZ............Simon UPTON</p>
<p>Finance, Government Superannuation Fund</p>
<p>    Department......................................Bill BIRCH</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs &amp; Trade, Pacific Island</p>
<p>    Affairs......................................See Deputy PM</p>
<p> Forestry, Racing.................................John FALLOON</p>
<p> Health, Women's Affairs.........................Jenny SHIPLEY</p>
<p>Housing, Customs, Associate Minister of</p>
<p>of Tourism Tourism, Sport, Local Government,</p>
<p>     Civil Defence..............................Murray MCCULLY</p>
<p>Justice, Courts, Treaty of Waitangi</p>
<p>Negotiations, Disarmament and</p>
<p>    Arms Control, Culture.......................Douglas GRAHAM</p>
<p>Labour, Fisheries, Energy, Accident</p>
<p>    Rehabilitation Compensation Insurance............Doug KIDD</p>
<p>Lands, Survey and Land Information,</p>
<p>in charge of Valuation Department,</p>
<p>Associate Minister of Agriculture and</p>
<p>    Associate Minister of Employment............Denis MARSHALL</p>
<p> Maori Affairs, Police, Commerce, Industry.........John LUXTON</p>
<p> Revenue, Internal Affairs.........................Peter DUNNE</p>
<p> Social Welfare, Senior Citizens.................Peter GRESHAM</p>
<p>Trade Negotiations, Associate Minister of</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs and Trade,</p>
<p>    State Owned Enterprises, Railways............Philip BURDON</p>
<p>Transport, Statistics, Communications,</p>
<p>Information Technology, Broadcasting,</p>
<p>    Associate Minister of Health............Maurice WILLIAMSON</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OUTSIDE CABINET:</p>
<p>Consumer Affairs, Associate Minister</p>
<p>of Women's Affairs, Associate Minister of Health,</p>
<p>Associate Minister of Social Welfare.....Katherine O'REGAN</p>
<p>Immigration, Business Development,</p>
<p>    Associate Minister of Employment.............Roger MAXWELL</p>
<p>State, Associate Minister Foreign Affairs</p>
<p>    and Trade.......................................Robin GRAY</p>
<p>Youth Affairs, Associate Minister of Education,</p>
<p>Social Welfare and Pacific Island Affairs.....Roger MCCLAY</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Speaker of the House of Representatives.........Peter TAPSELL</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Reserve Bank Governor...............................Don BRASH</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			 (End Government List)</p>
